$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=rectintce0  LOC_AFTER=?

* Cauchy estimate of order zero: the value of a holomorphic function at a strictly interior point is bounded by the maximum of its absolute value on the boundary frame, times the half perimeter over pi R, where R is below each coordinate gap.  The weak maximum modulus principle.

